<title>UK: U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 14,250 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 45.422 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Out of this, traders in France received 8,000 tonnes, in Belgium 6,000 and in Spain 250 tonnes, it added.  </p>
<p>This week's award brings the cumulative tonnage awarded for export from the 1996/97 crop to 1.397 million tonnes. This compares with the 39,823 tonnes awarded on January 24, 1995, when the cumulative tonnage totalled 1.548 million tonnes.</p>
<p>In its last tender on January 22, the EU awarded 36,600 tonnes at a maximum restitution of 46.281 Ecus.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
